Hotspot 0.05 - test against the real hotspot
============================================

Hotspot is a desktop controller for a WPSD hotspot. It uses the hotspot's
own web dashboard, so nothing is installed on the hotspot. It starts out
set to your hotspot's address, 10.0.0.27, and is aimed at the three things
you use: BrandMeister DMR, TGIF DMR and YSF.

Step by step
------------
1. Put the program on a local disc.
   Copy the !Hotspot folder from this folder (Development/Hotspot on the
   NAS) onto a local disc, or unzip Hotspot-0.05.zip there. Run it from the
   local copy, not from the share.

2. Start it.
   Double-click !Hotspot. The Hotspot icon appears on the icon bar, the
   main window opens and, because it is the first run, so does the
   "Hotspot choices" window.

3. Fill in the Choices window.
   Hotspot address ..... 10.0.0.27 (already there)
   Port ................ 80
   User name ........... pi-star
   Password ............ type the hotspot's Admin password
   Click Save. (Tab, or Return, moves from box to box; Return in the last
   box also saves.)

4. Look at the Status tab (within a few seconds).
   Expect "Connected." in green, then: the Radio section (IDLE, 438.780 MHz
   transmit, the modem type), Modes Enabled with DMR and YSF each having a
   Pause button, the DMR masters (BM 2341 United Kingdom, TGIF Network),
   YSF Status with "Link  GB-NWFG2", and the hardware figures at the end.
   If it says "Not connected" go to step 11.

5. Click the Heard tab.
   The last heard list. When someone is transmitting, their row turns green
   (it updates every few seconds).

6. Click the DMR tab.
   DMR networks: BM 2341 United Kingdom and TGIF Network, each with a
   Disable button. BrandMeister: the static talkgroups with Link/Drop/Delete
   buttons, Add TG..., and Drop QSO / Drop dynamic. TGIF: a row to link and
   unlink a talkgroup (it may say "current links not shown": see below).
   Try, one at a time, and watch the "Last action" line under the title:
   - Disable beside TGIF Network, wait about five seconds, then Enable.
   - Link or Drop a BrandMeister talkgroup you do not mind changing.
   - Link... on the TGIF row, type a talkgroup, click Link.

7. Click the Links tab.
   YSF reflector: "linked to GB-NWFG2" with Link... and Unlink buttons.
   Click Link..., type a YSF reflector number (for example 00001) and click
   Link. After a few seconds the row shows the new link and a "Recent YSF
   reflectors" row appears under it with a button for it: clicking that
   button links the same reflector again in one go. Put GB-NWFG2 back with
   Link... when finished.

8. Try Pause and Resume on the Status tab (Pause beside DMR or YSF; the
   button turns into Resume).

9. Press the Menu button over the window: Refresh, Modes, DMR, Links,
   System, View, Find hotspot..., Save diagnostics, Choices.

10. Press the Menu button over the icon bar icon: Info, Help..., Find
    hotspot..., Choices..., Quit (clicking the icon itself opens the window;
    Help... opens this kind of text file in your editor). The menu should sit
    exactly on top of the icon bar, not overlap it. Move the
    pointer onto the arrow beside Info: the "Program information" window
    opens beside the menu (Name, Purpose, Author, Version), as in other
    programs, and goes away with the menu.

11. If the hotspot's address ever changes.
    Click Find hotspot... (beside the "Not connected" message, in the
    window, or in either menu). The box starts with 10.0.0. - check it is
    the first three numbers of your network's addresses and click Search.
    After a few seconds each hotspot found is offered: "Found a hotspot at
    10.0.0.27 ... Use this address?" - click Continue. (If it finds the address
    you are already using it says so.) You can also just change the address
    in Choices.

12. If anything looks wrong, open the System tab and click Save beside
    "Save diagnostics report": the box tells you where the file is.
    Send it (or describe what you saw). The report holds what the hotspot
    answered to each request, never the password.

Notes
-----
* Looking at the hotspot needs no password; anything that changes it, and
  the DMR network and BrandMeister lists, use the Admin login.
* Your own settings are saved in your Choices directory and used instead of
  the ones shipped in the application.
* A fixed address for the hotspot in your router (a DHCP reservation) stops
  the address ever moving.
